  "reason": "With no prior evidence, I need to establish a strong baseline while testing the core multimodal hypothesis. config_012 (multimodal, multiprofile, pca_n2000, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) combines the strongest available image encoder (ViT-L pretrained on ImageNet) with a robust, low-variance RNA representation (PCA-2000), standard average pooling for multi-profile aggregation, and weighted fusion to allow learned modality balancing. This is a 'center-of-space' multimodal configuration likely to perform competitively. It establishes a performance anchor: if it scores well, subsequent experiments can probe which component (RNA encoder, aggregation strategy, fusion type) drives gains; if it underperforms, it signals that multimodal fusion itself or a specific component needs rethinking. Under a 10-experiment budget, anchoring with a strong prior is the highest-information first move."
